#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
slak - agent-native Slack CLI that acts as YOU.

Zero dependencies (Python 3.8+ stdlib only). Every command supports --json for
machine consumption. Designed to be driven by a human OR by an agent runtime.

Auth rides on the Slack desktop app: `slak login` decrypts its `d` session
cookie and mints an xoxc token from it, the same recipe as slk
(https://github.com/gammons/slk). No Slack App, no OAuth, no admin approval.
When the token goes stale it is re-minted from the cookie automatically.
The only non-Python piece is the `openssl` binary, for AES.
"""
